A method takes the value before the dot as its first parameter. Moth calls
that value the *receiver*. Declare the method as a top-level function in the
same file as the struct or choice and name its first parameter `this`.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    Player = | name String, score I32 = 0 |

    qualifies |this Player, minimum I32| -> Bool {
        return this.score >= minimum
    }

    player = Player("Priya", score = 10)
    can_enter = player.qualifies(8)
]

In the call, `player` supplies `this` and 8 supplies `minimum`. The method
reads the score and returns true. The shared receiver lets it read the player
without changing it. Call receiver methods with a dot, even in the file that
declares them.
